  "full_text": "I was not popular in school at all. I was kind of a geek. A real geek. Hugging the walls. Very shy. I'm still very shy. Couldn't really speak. I was blushing when a teacher was asking me a question. I was paralyzed. I was not good with boys. I've got a non-identical twin sister. She's not at all in the business. She lives in Italy. Married to an Italian count. She's blonde. It's the other me, you know, the happy me. I am so shy. And at the same time, I kind of expose myself literally to thousands of people. And, you know, this is my body. But I still don't really understand why I do that. And I go, I need to go through therapy. Being a Bond girl, I was like, oh my God, what is it a Bond girl do? You know, is it like wearing a bikini and being beautiful and that's it? Kind of was like, I was like, no, I'm not going to go. And I won't get it anyway, you know. And then they sent me the script, and I completely changed my mind, and I thought it was a very... It was a love story. I die a lot in movies. I don't know why. It's a big rehearsal. People have this image of me of being otherworldly, of being weird, that I could kind of communicate with the spirits. I don't know, maybe it's my dark hair or maybe because I don't talk much. So they kind of like put me in the like, whoa, whoa, whoa, weirdo box. I don't know. I'm human. You know, I'm not like this. Always admired. It's always been.",
